@@ -195,6 +196,26 @@ Waveform, stem and cue colors keep their meaning in every theme. Pick one under
 
 <p align="center"><img src="images/themes-day.png" width="640" alt="The waveform view in the Day theme"></p>
 
+### Hebrew
+
+The deck's own fonts have no Hebrew, so Hebrew track, playlist and folder names
+show up as boxes. With **Hebrew** on they show as Hebrew letters, in the deck's
+own text everywhere: browse lists, track info, decks.
+
+- **Right to Left**: Hebrew reads right to left, with English words and numbers
+  in their own order, so `שיר (Remix)` and `Artist - שיר` read the way you
+  typed them. A Hebrew name too long for its row is cut on the left, so its
+  beginning stays in view.
+- **Hebrew Keyboard**: the search keyboard opens in Hebrew. **123** switches it
+  to English, and **ABC** on the numbers page back to Hebrew.
+
+On Windows, the [Hebrew mod's launcher](https://github.com/meow3040/xdj-az-hebrew-mod)
+builds the mods with Hebrew, copies them to your USB stick and turns Hebrew on at the deck.
+Or turn it on under **Hebrew** in the Mod Menu and **Reload** once. Right to Left
+and the keyboard need firmware 2.00 or 2.01. The Hebrew letters come from the
+DejaVu Sans Bold font and are built into the mods: the deck's own font files are
+not changed.
+
